Confirmed. We lodged the entry on Friday using the code 0811.90 that was on t=
he supplier's pre-advice. We did not compare it with the invoice descriptions=
, which is our gap.

We can amend as soon as we have the right code. Please confirm 0710.80 (veget=
ables, frozen) is correct for both containers, and send the invoice lines. On=
ce the amendment is submitted, the system normally needs several hours to re-=
assess and the goods can then be released.

Best regards,
Harbour Agency UK
Customs agent Felixstowe

-----Original Message-----
From: Oliver Wright <o.wright@corp-europe.example>
Sent: Monday, 28 September 2026 10:05
To: Harbour Agency UK; Marta Kowalska
Subject: Reefers MSKU4021553 and TGHU7781204 held at Felixstowe

Both reefers came off the vessel this morning and are on customs hold: MSKU40=
21553 and TGHU7781204. The terminal says release is blocked because the impor=
t declaration shows commodity code 0811.90 (frozen fruit), while the invoice =
and packing list describe frozen vegetables.

Since Brexit reefers can't be released without a full import declaration, so =
we need a corrected one before anything moves. Both boxes are on reefer plug =
at the terminal and the clock on free time is running.

Harbour, can you check what you lodged and amend it today? Marta, please send=
 the corrected commodity code and the invoice lines as soon as you have them.

Kind regards,
Oliver Wright
